Z||000000||Jim Kempthorn||07-14-2000||02:00 PM||||I have an 84 Fiero.  The engine has been I been rebuilt with about 3000 miles.  I have gone through 3 alternator belts.  Has anyone had a similar problem and a possible cause and solution.<P>Thanks,<P>Jim ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Taijiguy||07-14-2000||02:14 PM||||Check for pulley alignment, and also inspect the pulleys for burrs and other rough spots/abrasions. If all else fails, tow it to my house and park it there. I'l get it back to you at some point. Oh yeah,make sure you leave the keys!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Taiji||||reg||1
Z||000002||moonie||07-14-2000||02:34 PM||||i put on a new alt belt about every 2 weeks .<BR>my lower main pulley is warped.<P>will order one soon , but heck , belt is 3 bucks & can be changed in 15 minutes(practice makes perfect )<BR>when it breaks , i look like a pir crew on a ernie irvan car ....parts flying & wrenches turning. wife won't let me have a reciprocating ( wooo ) saw to cut stuff with though . <BR>she reads a book , i change belt & we're gone .....<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||07-15-2000||01:37 PM||||Try a diferant brand of belt. Dayco belts stink. I've seen brand new ones of theirs die in days. Try Gates. You may have to order them from Carparts.com or someone. Not allot of places stock them for some reason.||||reg||1
